---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Use"
  kicker="Legal"
  heading="Terms of Use"
  lede="The terms that govern this website, PRC's educational materials, memberships, and orders. Effective August 2, 2026."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        By using paularecordscustodian.com, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the site. "PRC" means Paula Records Custodian LLC.
      </p>

      <h2>Educational content — not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Everything published on this site — checklists, guides, e-books, request-letter templates,
        and the Request Builder — is general educational information about records commonly
        associated with events, processes, agencies, disputes, and transitions. It is not legal,
        tax, accounting, medical, or social-work advice, and using it does not create a
        professional-client relationship of any kind. Requirements vary by state, agency, and
        situation; confirm exact requirements with the appropriate attorney, accountant, agency,
        court, insurer, lender, healthcare professional, or other qualified source. PRC's full
        scope commitments are in our <a href="/service-boundaries">Service Boundaries</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Services and written scope</h2>
      <p>
        PRC services are provided only under a written engagement with a defined scope — entities,
        properties, units, accounts, transactions, documents, users, storage volume, and review
        complexity. Published prices are starting points; the written scope controls. Nothing on
        this website constitutes an engagement, and no engagement begins until both parties approve
        the written scope. PRC does not guarantee legal, tax, regulatory, funding, lending,
        insurance, or compliance outcomes.
      </p>

      <h2>Orders</h2>
      <p>
        Product orders placed through this site are requests, not completed purchases. PRC confirms
        the total (including shipping) and payment options by email before anything is charged, and
        either party may cancel before payment. Defective or damaged items will be replaced or
        refunded — email us within 30 days of delivery.
      </p>

      <h2>Library membership</h2>
      <p>
        Records Readiness Library access codes are personal and non-transferable. Membership
        content is for your own use; sharing codes or redistributing member content ends the
        membership. Memberships run for their stated term; PRC will honor the full paid term or
        refund the unused portion if the Library is ever discontinued.
      </p>

      <h2>Client portal</h2>
      <p>
        Portal access codes identify your engagement — keep them private and tell us immediately
        if one may be compromised, and we will replace it. The portal shows engagement status and
        updates; it is not a document-exchange channel, and our
        <a href="/records-handling">Records Handling Notice</a> explains why.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Don't misuse the site: no attempts to access other people's records or accounts, probe or
        overload the systems, submit false or unlawful content through forms, or use automated
        tools to scrape member content.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The PRC name, the PRC Records Readiness Framework, and the content of this site belong to
        Paula Records Custodian LLC. Free resources may be used and printed for personal,
        non-commercial purposes with attribution intact. Redistribution or commercial use —
        including of member content — requires written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The website and its educational materials are provided "as is," without warranties of any
        kind. To the fullest extent permitted by law, PRC's total liability arising from your use
        of this website or its free materials is limited to $100; liability connected to a paid
        engagement, order, or membership is limited to the amount you paid for it. Nothing in
        these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, without regard to conflict-of-law
        rules. Disputes will be resolved in the state or federal courts located in Texas.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Updated terms will be posted here with a new effective date; continued use of the site
        after a change means acceptance. Contact: <strong>contact@paularecordscustodian.com</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
